  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Pennsylvania State University has $354M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. Pennsylvania State University received 207 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $1.7M. Pennsylvania State University obligations are up 2.6% year over year. The Department of Defense is the primary buyer, obligating $351M. Research work drives most of the activity, led by Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) at $352M. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration and the Department of the Interior are smaller buyers with recorded obligations. Other research markets and university services contribute more modest totals, including Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities and Colleges, Universities, and Professional Schools. Current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress.",
    "sections": [
