        "heading": "Who are Pennsylvania State University's main federal buyers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the main buyer, obligating $351M. The National Aeronautics and Space Administration obligated $2M, and the Department of the Interior obligated $1.1M. Several other agencies have smaller or limited recorded activity."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and contract types drive Pennsylvania State University's federal revenue?",
        "body": "Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest market at $352M. Additional research categories and university services include Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences, Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities at $469K, and Colleges, Universities, and Professional Schools at $70.8K."
      }
    ]
